{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]Deep are [Ab]the wounds [Ab7]transgression has made;
[Db]Red [Gb]are the [Db]stains; [Ab7]my soul [Db]is afraid.
[Ab7][Db]O [Gb]to [Gb]be [Db][Eb]covered, [Eb7]Jesus, [Ab]with [Ab7]Thee,
[Db]Safe [Gb]from the [Db]law [Ab7]that now [Db]judgeth me!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]Longing the [Ab]joy of [Ab7]pardon to know;
[Db]Jesus [Gb]holds out [Db]a [Ab7]robe white [Db]as snow;
[Ab7][Db]"Lord, [Gb]I [Gb]accept [Db][Eb]it! [Eb7]Leaving [Ab]my [Ab7]own,
[Db]Gladly [Gb]I [Db]wear Thy [Ab7]pure [Db]life alone."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]Reconciled by [Ab]His death [Ab7]for my sin,
[Db]Justified [Gb]by [Db]His life [Ab7]pure [Db]and clean,
[Ab7][Db]Sanctified [Gb][Gb]by [Db][Eb]obeying [Eb7][Ab]His [Ab7]word,
[Db]Glorified [Gb]when [Db]returneth [Ab7]my [Db]Lord.
